        "orario": "17:41",
        "timestamp": 1776094904,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Deadline passes for US blockade of Hormuz, Iran threatens to retaliate against Gulf neighbours Issued on: 13/04/2026 - 17:41 The deadline passed on Monday for the start of a US ​military blockade of ships leaving Iran's ports, and Tehran threatened to retaliate against ports of its Gulf neighbours after weekend talks on ending the war broke down. Oil prices surged, with no sign of a swift reopening of the Strait of Hormuz to ease the biggest ever disruption in supplies. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more. Hungarians look to changed future after pro-EU Magyar's election landslide 13/04/2026 Pro-EU Hungarian PM-elect Magyar vows to bring in 'new era' 13/04/2026 Hungary's Orban defeated: France's far-right loses an ally 13/04/2026 US-Vatican feud over Iran: Pope Leo pushes back on Trump's criticism 13/04/2026 French lawmakers to debate bill to return looted colonial-era art 13/04/2026 US says to blockade Iran ports: What could be the consequences? 13/04/2026 Electoral earthquake: Hungary vote triggers setback for Putin and Trump 13/04/2026 In Bangladesh, bus drivers taking enormous risks to go fast and furious 13/04/2026 Hungarian election: EU leaders celebrate Peter Magyar's victory 13/04/2026"
